                <pb facs="0829" n="731" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg731"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Baron
                            Fava.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-11-27"><hi rendition="#italic">November 27,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear</hi> Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Ambassador</hi>: Answering your personal communication of the 26th, I have
                    the pleasure to inform you that the subject of the Tallulah lynchings and the
                    question of providing a Federal forum for such cases, concerning which you have
                    heretofore conferred with me, have been duty considered by the President and
                    will be appropriately treated in his forthcoming message.</p>
                <p>Believe me to be, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
